# cw137, the disputed well (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw137
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_delphine_sootley
written_by claude-codex-cw-2
title the disputed well
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=plain
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk cannot_resist_a_wager
likes oatcakes whittling old_maps thunder
dislikes waiting salt_wind
fears the_well_claimed_by_one_house a_wager_that_costs_the_yard
hopes a_fair_turn_at_the_well steady_work_through_winter
topics work +0.4 prices +0.3 pastimes +0.3 weather +0.3 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=reserved gossip=guarded refuse=direct tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# wagers on the #weather#, whittles a #peg# beside the #fire#, and watches who takes #water# from the common #well#.

words
oath! = Well and wager | By the unclaimed bucket
saying! = A shared well takes turns | Never bet the feed money
wager = wager | small bet
bet = bet | wager
coin = coin | penny
well = well | common well
water = water | clear water
bucket = bucket | well bucket
buckets = buckets | well buckets
rope = rope | well rope
turn = turn | fair turn
turns = turns | fair turns
line = line | waiting line
neighbour = neighbour | next-door neighbour
pig = pig | yard pig
pigs = pigs | yard pigs
yard = yard | pig yard
pen = pen | pig pen
trough = trough | feed trough
feed = feed | mash
straw = straw | dry bedding
gate = gate | yard gate
mud = mud | wet mud
boots = boots | work boots
oatcake = oatcake | oatcake with butter
oatcakes = oatcakes | buttered oatcakes
butter = butter | fresh butter
knife = knife | whittling knife
wood = wood | scrap wood
peg = peg | whittled peg
fire = fire | hearth fire
map = map | old map
maps = maps | old maps
road = road | High Road
city = city | Ridgemere
roof = roof | sound roof
thunder = thunder | thunderstorm
cloud = cloud | storm cloud
wind = wind | salt wind
lake = lake | Glasswater
shore = shore | lake shore
market = market | market square
bread = bread | loaf
price = price | asking price
home = home | cottage
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | working hands
time = time | spare hour
count = count | careful tally
sun = sun | winter sun

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : The #city# would put a lock on a shared #well#. | I trust a #road# on an old #map# more than a city's promise.
opinion @1 dole against 1 : I want another #bucket# of work before a queue. | A full #trough# comes from someone carrying #feed#.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : They would fence the #well# and charge a #coin# for the key. | I know what an empty bench looks like from their side.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : They raise the #bread# #price# even when my #coin# has not changed. | I make them state the cost before I open my purse.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : A new worker takes a #turn# I waited for. | I will still teach the #gate# rule if they stay.
opinion @1 strangers against 2 : A stranger can draw #water# after the locals take their #turn#. | My #home# door stays shut until I know their name.
opinion @1 times against 1 : It takes another #coin# to fill the #feed# #bucket# each month. | The #market# does not wait for my wages.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : Let the Watch hear both sides of the #well# dispute. | They can count #buckets# if they have no better task.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. Are you here about the #well#? | #greet#. Keep clear of the #pen# #gate#.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Speak while I fill the #trough#. | My #bucket# must reach the #pen# first.
line @3 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I have #oatcakes# by the #fire#. | You may see the #peg# I just cut.
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : The first #bucket# is already at the #well#. | #greet#. The #pigs# woke early.
line @1 greet.return : #welcome_back#. Has the #well# settled itself yet? | You have found me with another #map#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come in; leave your #boots# near the #fire#. | Take an #oatcake# before it cools.
line @1 again.open : We left the #wager# unresolved. | Have you come with news of the #well#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Keep your #bucket# upright. | #saying.capitalize#. Shut the #gate#.
line @1 farewell.return : I may have finished this #peg# by then. | Another #oatcake# will be waiting.
line @1 react.news : I will listen before placing a #wager#. | Tell me who drew from the #well#.
line @1 react.news.new : No one has said that at this #yard#. | Did it come from the #market#?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard a different part beside the #well#. | Your detail changes how I understood it.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #hedge#, I want to see the #bucket# marks myself. | A person can count turns to suit an argument.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That is grim. Sit inside by the #fire#. | Let me leave this #knife# and listen properly.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. That deserves fresh #oatcakes#. | I would wager this news will lift the whole #home#.
line @1 answer.how : The #pigs# are fed; the #well# is another matter. | Waiting less than yesterday, which is something.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I have #feed# to mix and #straw# to change. | The #trough# needs filling before any debate.
line @1 ask.how : Did you get your #turn# at the #well#? | Have you eaten?
line @1 sympathise : I can spare a #time# by the #fire#. | I will keep this between us.
line @1 reassure : We can count the #buckets# together tomorrow. | The #gate# will be mended before another #pig# escapes.
line @1 decline : No; the #feed# money belongs to the #pigs#. | I must stay while the #yard# is open.
line @1 accept_decline : Then the #coin# stays in my pocket. | I hear your answer.
line @1 thank : You returned the #bucket# before the #pigs# needed it. | I saw you close the #gate# properly.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I cut a #peg# from spare #wood#. | The #oatcakes# were already warm.
line @1 preclose : I must check the #well# #rope# before dusk. | The #pigs# need another #count#.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You would wager on a #cloud# you cannot see. | That #map# is straighter than the #road#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. I will take my #turn# later. | #bc_fair_enough#. The #bucket# is yours.
line @1 give.advice : Draw #water# with both #hands# on the #rope#. | Never stake the #coin# for #feed#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : The #road# is no place for a loose #coin# tonight. | Bring a friend if you must fetch #water# after dark.
scene common_well
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #well# belongs to everyone who hauls a #bucket#. | I count the #turns# when the morning #line# forms.
b : Has anyone claimed it? | Who goes first?
a : Someone tries now and then. | The person who came early.

scene neighbour_turn
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #neighbour# and I disagree over who had the first #bucket#. | The #well# itself has given no opinion.
b : Could you share a schedule? | Are you speaking now?
a : We could, if we agreed where it began. | About the weather.

scene well_rope
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I test the #rope# before lowering the #bucket#. | A frayed length can leave the #water# beyond reach.
b : Has it snapped? | Can you replace it?
a : Not on my turn. | I have a coil ready.

scene small_wager
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I wagered an #oatcake# on which #pig# would reach the #gate# first. | The slow one won after the others stopped for #feed#.
b : Who took the cake? | Do you bet often?
a : A friend who knew the #pigs#. | More than I should.

scene thunder_roof
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like #thunder# from beneath a sound #roof#. | The #pigs# settle if the #fire# is steady.
b : Does it frighten them? | Would you go outside?
a : The young ones. | For the #gate#, if needed.

scene salt_wind
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #wind# off the #lake# leaves salt on my mouth. | I turn my face away when the #shore# air sharpens.
b : Does it reach the yard? | Do you close the door?
a : On clear days. | If it blows into the #home#.

scene map_error
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My old #map# sends a #road# over a patch of #lake#. | I keep the mistake; it makes the rest easier to question.
b : Who drew it? | Would you follow any route on it?
a : No name remains. | Only after walking it myself.

scene whittled_peg
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I whittle a #peg# from spare #wood# while the #fire# burns low. | A useful #peg# is better than a pretty carving.
b : What is it for? | Do you make many?
a : The #gate# latch. | Whenever the #knife# is sharp.

scene oatcake_butter
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An #oatcake# wants #butter# before it cools. | I save one for after the #yard# is clean.
b : Do you bake them? | How many do you eat?
a : When I have the oats. | Enough to stay at work.

scene waiting_line
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #line# at the #well# can steal an hour from the #yard#. | I bring two #buckets# and save a second journey.
b : Does that upset people? | Can you go earlier?
a : Only if I take another's #turn#. | Before dawn, sometimes.

scene pen_feed
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I put the #feed# into the #trough# before opening the #pen#. | Otherwise the #pigs# rush the #bucket#.
b : Do they knock you over? | How do you hold them?
a : They have tried. | With a firm #gate#.

scene dry_straw
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Dry #straw# keeps the #pen# sound when the #mud# rises. | I change the bedding before the #pigs# complain.
b : How do they complain? | Do you have enough straw?
a : Loudly. | For this week.

scene bad_gate
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #gate# latch slipped when a #pig# leaned on it. | I carved a new #peg# to hold it shut.
b : Did the pig escape? | Will the peg last?
a : Only to the #yard#. | Until I can fit iron.

scene first_coin
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep the first #coin# of a day's wages out of my wagers. | A foolish #bet# should not empty the #trough#.
b : Is that difficult? | Do you ever win?
a : When the odds look good. | Often enough to keep trying.

scene market_bread
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I ask the #bread# seller why the #price# rose before handing over #coin#. | A clear answer is better than a long argument.
b : Do you get one? | Do you buy anyway?
a : Rarely. | When the #home# needs it.

scene shared_house
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #home# is full of orchard workers and their #boots#. | I keep my #knife# and #maps# on the high shelf.
b : Is it noisy? | Do you share meals?
a : At the end of the day. | When our hours meet.

scene winter_well
when topic=weather here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Ice gathers on the #well# #rope# before the #sun# reaches it. | I break the crust before lowering a #bucket#.
b : Is the water colder? | Does the queue grow?
a : It feels so through the handle. | When everyone waits for light.

story contested_bucket [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I set my #bucket# at the #well# before dawn.
  : Another hand arrived and said the place had been saved earlier.
  ask : Who drew first?
  b : A common well needs a clear order.
  : We argued, then drew for both households and spoke less afterward.

story pig_wager [topic=pastimes self.age>=25]
  : I wagered an #oatcake# on a #pig# reaching the #gate# first.
  : It stopped for fallen #feed# and another passed.
  ask : Did you pay?
  b : The pig had not heard your bet.
  : I paid, and ate my next #oatcake# without a wager.

story map_water [topic=pastimes self.age>=25]
  : A faded #map# put a #road# across part of the #lake#.
  : I took it to the #shore# and compared ink with the water.
  ask : Did you correct it?
  b : The lake was unlikely to move.
  : I drew the true #shore# beside the old line.

rule @bark_well
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say My #bucket# was here first. | The #well# belongs to all of us.

rule @bark_wager
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say One #oatcake# says that #cloud# will break. | No, not the #feed# #coin#.

rule @bark_pigs
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say The #trough# needs another #bucket#. | Keep the #pigs# behind the #gate#.

rule @bark_wood
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 11h
say This #peg# is nearly finished. | The #fire# is low enough to whittle by.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I am fetching #water# before the #pigs# wake. | #greet#. Stay clear while I swing the #gate#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You have found the #well# busy again. | Back? I still have that #map# by the #fire#.
dlg @1 resident.job : At #self.workplace# I haul #water# and feed the #pigs#. | I feed the #pen#, keep #straw# dry, and fix the #gate#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Leave the #bucket# by the #well#. | #saying.capitalize#. The #yard# needs me.
graft resident.hub
choice Who owns the well? -> well
node well
say Everyone who draws from it, which is the trouble. I want a fair #turn#.
free
choice What are you whittling? -> peg
choice Back to the yard. -> hub
node peg
say A #peg# for the #gate# latch. If it holds, I owe the #pig# no thanks.
choice Back to the yard. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
